00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.990 align:start position:0%
they had been buried alive  two weeks in the dark freezing  underground 600 meters down  this was the first miner returned to the  surface  his eyes blindfolded against the glare  of a sun not seen for a fortnight  one by one they were raised up and  delivered to safety  some were too weak to walk carried to  one of the 25 ambulances standing by  at the scene the first communication  from the trapped miners  received a week ago was a note saying  please don't stop  trying to reach us  and you can see just how thankful this  miner was that they did not  the rescuers checked the miners to see  if they had any injuries  and covered their eyes for protection  generally speaking  the rescue operation proceeded faster  than expected  after lifting all the trap miners  discovered we'll go on with the search  for other missing miners  on the 10th of january an explosion  blocked the main shaft at the hushan  gold mine in shandong province east  china  the mine entrance was blocked 350 meters  below the surface  by 70 tons of debris reaching down 100  meters  rescuers made contact with the miners by  drilling narrow shafts  sending telephones food and medicine  down  then they drilled a new wider shaft to  reach the miners trapped in the  midsection of the tunnel below  and bring them to the surface one miner  was confirmed dead from a head injury  others were in a bad state and they were  brought up first  the critical cases come before the  others it's the principle of mine  accident rescue  so the severe ones have been pulled up  first and the following are in better  physical and psychological condition  this is an ongoing rescue operation  though several miners are still  unaccounted for  they drilled more holes to try and reach  them and if they do find them  to send down food to try and keep them  alive and strong  china's mining industry has a terrible  safety record there have been multiple  deaths over the last two years alone  it is grimly unsurprising when a fatal  mining accident occurs  it is a miracle when like today people  survive  tom chester sky news beijing
 

